      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>House Rent Allowance (HRA) Classification Across Maharashtra Cities</h2>
        <p>
          In Maharashtra, House Rent Allowance is administered based on population density under state financial rules, directly reflecting high urban living expenses:
        </p>

        <div class="city-classification-grid">
          <div class="city-box tier-x">
            <h4>Class X (Metropolitan Areas)</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Mumbai MMR, Thane, Pune MMR</div>
            <p><strong>Baseline HRA Rate:</strong> 27% of Basic Pay (Projected up to 30%).</p>
            <p><strong>Covered Municipalities:</strong> Greater Mumbai (BMC), Navi Mumbai, Thane, Pune (PMC), and Pimpri-Chinchwad (PCMC).</p>
            <span class="card-footer-note">Reflects the highest residential rental cost bracket in the country.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="city-box tier-y">
            <h4>Class Y (Major Urban Corporations)</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Population 5 Lakh to 50 Lakh</div>
